Author: indbakasensei <indian.baka.sensei01@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Jul 13 12:01:09 2026 +0000

    fix(scheduler): configure JobQueue timezone for IST daily schedules
    
    Application never set Defaults(tzinfo=...), so JobQueue's underlying
    APScheduler defaulted to UTC. Every run_daily() job (carry-forward,
    evening review, morning briefing, weekly report, observation engine,
    project nudges) fired 5.5 hours later than intended local time.
    
    Fix verified against the installed python-telegram-bot 20.7 source:
    JobQueue.set_application() reads application.bot.defaults.tzinfo,
    falling back to pytz.utc when unset. Uses pytz.timezone (not
    zoneinfo.ZoneInfo) since JobQueue calls .localize() on the configured
    tzinfo internally. No scheduling logic changed.
    
    Resolves ENGINEERING_AUDIT.md finding D1 (CRITICAL).
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

